  "articleBody": "Nobody wants their new tile floor to start failing shortly after it's installed, right? There are some common blunders folks make that can lead to big headaches. Here’s how to steer clear of them:\n\n1. Poor Subfloor Prep: This is a huge one! If your subfloor isn’t clean, level, and structurally sound, your tiles won’t last. Always take the time to prepare the base properly, or have a pro handle it.\n\n2. Ignoring Moisture Issues: Especially in places like bathrooms or basements, moisture can wreak havoc on tile. Make sure any water problems are resolved before tiling, and use appropriate waterproofing if necessary.\n\n3. Forgetting Movement Joints: Floors naturally expand and contract. Without proper expansion joints, your tiles can crack or buckle. A skilled installer knows where to place these critical gaps.\n\n4. Tiling Over Problematic Existing Tile: Just because you can, doesn't mean you should. Tiling over old, loose, or uneven tile is a recipe for disaster. It's usually best to remove the old stuff and start with a fresh surface.\n\n5. Using the Wrong Adhesive or Grout: Not all mortars and grouts are created equal. Different tiles and environments require specific products for optimal performance. Don't just grab the cheapest option; use what's right for the job. Avoiding these pitfalls can save you a lot of time and money, and ensure your beautiful new floor stands the test of time. If any of this feels like too much, it's a good sign to call in the experts at HH Remodeling LLC; we've got the experience to prevent these issues.",
